  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vikas Panditrao Mandi vs The State Of Maharashtra on 13 May, 2019 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 20.Ba 131 Wakodikar In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.1314 Of 2019 Vikas Panditrao Mandi .... Applicant. V/s. The State of Maharashtra .... Respondents. Mr.Rahul Sopanrao Kate, for the applicant. App, Mr.S.R.Shinde for the State. Investigating Officer, Mr.Ratnadeep Salokhe present. Coram : N. J. Jamadar, J. (Vacation Court) Dated : 13th May, 2019. P.C. : 1. This is an application under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure for enlarging the applicant on bail. 2 . The applicant has been arraigned for the offences punishable under Section 188, 272, 273, 328 of Indian Penal Code and Section 26 (2), 26(2)(iv), 27 read with Section 30(2)(A) of Food Safety and Standards Act for having been found in possession of the contraband article i.e. Panmasala.",
    "facts": "This is an application under Section 439 of the Code of Criminal Procedure for enlarging the applicant on bail. 2 . The applicant has been arraigned for the offences punishable under Section 188, 272, 273, 328 of Indian Penal Code and Section 26 (2), 26(2)(iv), 27 read with Section 30(2)(A) of Food Safety and Standards Act for having been found in possession of the contraband article i.e. Panmasala. The substance of the prosecution is that on 25/03/2019, Smt.Meghna Pawar, Food Safety Officer, accompanied by the Police intercepted a container bearing registration No. RJ14 JK 3895. Upon search of the said container, it was found that it contained scented panmasala; the manufacture, sale, storage, transportation of which has been prohibited in the State of Maharashtra 1/3 Vikas Panditrao Mandi vs The State Of Maharashtra on 13 May, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/99526607/ 1 ::: Uploaded on - 13/05/2019 ::: Downloaded on - 14/05/2 20.BA 1 vide Government Resolution dated 20/07/2018. It transpired that the said container was being driven by Nawab Shaukatali Taumar. It was dispatched by Subhash Sharma, owner of Mahalaxmi Transport. The contraband material was to be unloaded in the godown of the applicant. The said material was, thereafter, to be collected by Mahesh Nanwani. The applicant/accused was apprehended from in front of the said godown premises. Upon the first information report lodged by Satish Subhashrao Hake, Food Safety Officer, the applicant came to be arrested on 26/03/2019. 3. The applicant contends that he has been falsely implicated in the said crime. The applicant is not the owner of the godown in question where the prohibited material was to be unloaded. applicant has no concern with the alleged transportation, storage and sale of the prohibited material. Hence, the applicant be released on bail. 4. The Investigating Officer Ratnadeep Salokhe has filed an affidavit in reply.",
